Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: cwu50: clear "prepared" even when DCS shutdown fails

cwu50_unprepare() returns early if either DCS command fails, leaving
ctx->prepared set. cwu50_prepare() then short-circuits on

	if (ctx->prepared)
		return 0;

so cwu50_prepare_cm45() is never called again and the panel is never
re-initialised for the rest of the boot. The display stays dark through
every subsequent modeset.

Those DCS writes do fail in practice: on RP1 the bridge's post_disable
runs rp1dsi_dsi_stop() before the panel's unprepare, so there is no live
DSI link left to carry them. The panel is being powered down either way,
so a failed courtesy shutdown must not prevent the driver from admitting
that it happened.

The CM3 branch in this same function already handles it correctly -- it
warns, jumps to the hardware reset, and always clears the flag. Give the
CM4/CM5 branch the same structure. cwu50_prepare_cm45() re-runs the full
sequence (regulators, optional RESX cycle, TE, SLPOUT and the init table),
so clearing the flag is sufficient to make the panel recoverable.

Observed on a ClockworkPi uConsole with CM5: `drm_panel` disable, whether
from DPMS off or from an s2idle resume, left the panel permanently dark
while the rest of the system kept running.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-cwu50.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-cwu50.c
@@ -610,15 +610,16 @@
 	/* CM4/CM5 path (unchanged from the original multi-panel driver) */
 	ret = mipi_dsi_dcs_set_display_off(dsi);
 	if (ret) {
-		dev_err(ctx->dev, "failed to turn display off (%d)\n", ret);
-		return ret;
+		dev_warn(ctx->dev, "failed to turn display off (%d)\n", ret);
+		goto cm45_done;
 	}
 
 	ret = mipi_dsi_dcs_enter_sleep_mode(dsi);
 	if (ret) {
-		dev_err(ctx->dev, "failed to enter sleep mode (%d)\n", ret);
-		return ret;
+		dev_warn(ctx->dev, "failed to enter sleep mode (%d)\n", ret);
+		goto cm45_done;
 	}
 	msleep(120);
 
+cm45_done:
 	if (!ctx->is_new_panel) {
